    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    # Read H_A, W_A\n    idx = 0\n    H_A, W_A = map(int, data[idx].split())\n    idx += 1\n    A = []\n    for _ in range(H_A):\n        A.append(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n    \n    # Read H_B, W_B\n    H_B, W_B = map(int, data[idx].split())\n    idx += 1\n    B = []\n    for _ in range(H_B):\n        B.append(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n    \n    # Read H_X, W_X\n    H_X, W_X = map(int, data[idx].split())\n    idx += 1\n    X = []\n    for _ in range(H_X):\n        X.append(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n    \n    # Find positions of black squares in A, B, and X\n    def get_black_positions(grid, h, w):\n        positions = []\n        for i in range(h):\n            for j in range(w):\n                if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                    positions.append((i, j))\n        return positions\n    \n    A_blacks = get_black_positions(A, H_A, W_A)\n    B_blacks = get_black_positions(B, H_B, W_B)\n    X_blacks = set(get_black_positions(X, H_X, W_X))\n    \n    # If the number of black squares in X is less than total black squares in A and B, impossible\n    if len(X_blacks) < len(A_blacks) + len(B_blacks):\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    # Try all possible translations for A and B relative to the X grid\n    # We will try to place the top-left corner of A at various offsets relative to X\n    # and similarly for B\n    \n    # Try every possible placement of A such that its black squares lie within X\n    possible_A_offsets = []\n    for dy in range(-H_A + 1, H_X):\n        for dx in range(-W_A + 1, W_X):\n            valid = True\n            transformed_A = []\n            for i, j in A_blacks:\n                ni, nj = i + dy, j + dx\n                if 0 <= ni < H_X and 0 <= nj < W_X:\n                    transformed_A.append((ni, nj))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid:\n                possible_A_offsets.append((dy, dx, set(transformed_A)))\n    \n    # Similarly for B\n    possible_B_offsets = []\n    for dy in range(-H_B + 1, H_X):\n        for dx in range(-W_B + 1, W_X):\n            valid = True\n            transformed_B = []\n            for i, j in B_blacks:\n                ni, nj = i + dy, j + dx\n                if 0 <= ni < H_X and 0 <= nj < W_X:\n                    transformed_B.append((ni, nj))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid:\n                possible_B_offsets.append((dy, dx, set(transformed_B)))\n    \n    # Check if there exists a pair of placements such that:\n    # 1. Union of black squares from A and B matches exactly the black squares in X\n    found = False\n    for a_dy, a_dx, a_set in possible_A_offsets:\n        for b_dy, b_dx, b_set in possible_B_offsets:\n            union_blacks = a_set | b_set\n            if union_blacks == X_blacks:\n                found = True\n                break\n        if found:\n            break\n    \n    print(\"Yes\" if found else \"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
