      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef solve():\n    V1, V2, V3 = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # Side length of cube\n    L = 7\n    total_volume_one_cube = L ** 3  # 343\n    \n    # We'll try to find a configuration of three cubes that satisfies the volume conditions.\n    # We fix the first cube at (0, 0, 0) without loss of generality (we can shift everything).\n    # Then we try small relative offsets for the other two cubes within a reasonable range.\n    # Since coordinates must be within [-100, 100], and we fix first cube at (0,0,0), others can be in [-100,100].\n    \n    # But to make it efficient, we limit search to small offsets (e.g., -10 to 15), since larger overlaps\n    # or gaps won't help meet exact volume conditions.\n    \n    def intersect(a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, c2):\n        # Returns the volume of intersection of two cubes\n        dx = max(0, min(a1+L, a2+L) - max(a1, a2))\n        dy = max(0, min(b1+L, b2+L) - max(b1, b2))\n        dz = max(0, min(c1+L, c2+L) - max(c1, c2))\n        return dx * dy * dz\n\n    def intersect3(a1,b1,c1, a2,b2,c2, a3,b3,c3):\n        # Volume of intersection of three cubes\n        dx = max(0, min(a1+L, a2+L, a3+L) - max(a1, a2, a3))\n        dy = max(0, min(b1+L, b2+L, b3+L) - max(b1, b2, b3))\n        dz = max(0, min(c1+L, c2+L, c3+L) - max(c1, c2, c3))\n        return dx * dy * dz\n\n    # Fix first cube at (0, 0, 0)\n    a1, b1, c1 = 0, 0, 0\n\n    # Try possible positions for second and third cube\n    # We search in a limited range around the first cube\n    for da2, db2, dc2 in product(range(-10, 15), repeat=3):\n        a2, b2, c2 = da2, db2, dc2\n        vol12 = intersect(a1,b1,c1, a2,b2,c2)\n        if vol12 > V2 + V3:  # Can't have more triple overlap than total double\n            continue\n        \n        for da3, db3, dc3 in product(range(-10, 15), repeat=3):\n            a3, b3, c3 = da3, db3, dc3\n            \n            vol13 = intersect(a1,b1,c1, a3,b3,c3)\n            vol23 = intersect(a2,b2,c2, a3,b3,c3)\n            vol123 = intersect3(a1,b1,c1, a2,b2,c2, a3,b3,c3)\n            \n            # Volume in exactly two cubes: (1∩2) + (1∩3) + (2∩3) - 3*(1∩2∩3)\n            exact_two = vol12 + vol13 + vol23 - 3 * vol123\n            \n            # Volume in all three\n            exact_three = vol123\n            \n            # Volume in exactly one:\n            # Each cube contributes its own volume minus overlaps\n            one1 = total_volume_one_cube - (vol12 + vol13 - vol123)\n            one2 = total_volume_one_cube - (vol12 + vol23 - vol123)\n            one3 = total_volume_one_cube - (vol13 + vol23 - vol123)\n            exact_one = one1 + one2 + one3\n            \n            if exact_one == V1 and exact_two == V2 and exact_three == V3:\n                # Found a solution\n                print(\"Yes\")\n                print(a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, c2, a3, b3, c3)\n                return\n    \n    # If no solution found\n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
