      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    if not data:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Build adjacency list\n    graph = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    edges = []\n    \n    index = 2\n    for _ in range(m):\n        u = int(data[index])\n        v = int(data[index + 1])\n        w = int(data[index + 2])\n        index += 3\n        graph[u].append((v, w))\n        edges.append((u, v, w))\n    \n    # Use Floyd-Warshall to compute shortest path between all pairs\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Initialize distances\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n    \n    for u, v, w in edges:\n        dist[u][v] = min(dist[u][v], w)\n    \n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            if dist[i][k] == INF:\n                continue\n            for j in range(1, n + 1):\n                if dist[k][j] != INF:\n                    dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])\n    \n    # Check if all vertices are reachable from at least one vertex\n    # For each vertex, check if we can reach all other vertices\n    valid_start = []\n    \n    for start in range(1, n + 1):\n        reachable = 0\n        for end in range(1, n + 1):\n            if dist[start][end] != INF:\n                reachable += 1\n        if reachable == n:\n            valid_start.append(start)\n    \n    if not valid_start:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    # Now we need to find the minimum weight walk that visits all vertices\n    # Since N <= 20, we can use TSP-like DP with bitmasks\n    # But we need to consider that we can start anywhere and use shortest paths\n    \n    # Check if the entire graph is strongly connected\n    strongly_connected = True\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            if dist[i][j] == INF:\n                strongly_connected = False\n                break\n        if not strongly_connected:\n            break\n    \n    if not strongly_connected:\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    # If we can reach every vertex from every other vertex, then we can form a walk\n    # We want to find the minimum cost to visit all vertices at least once\n    # This is equivalent to finding a minimum cost Hamiltonian path in the complete\n    # graph with edge weights given by shortest paths\n    \n    # Use TSP DP: dp[mask][i] = minimum cost to visit all vertices in mask, ending at vertex i\n    N = n\n    dp = [[INF] * (N + 1) for _ in range(1 << N)]\n    \n    # Initialize: start at each vertex\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        dp[1 << (i - 1)][i] = 0\n    \n    # Fill DP table\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << N):\n        for u in range(1, N + 1):\n            if dp[mask][u] == INF or not (mask & (1 << (u - 1))):\n                continue\n            for v in range(1, N + 1):\n                if mask & (1 << (v - 1)):  # already visited\n                    continue\n                new_mask = mask | (1 << (v - 1))\n                new_cost = dp[mask][u] + dist[u][v]\n                if new_cost < dp[new_mask][v]:\n                    dp[new_mask][v] = new_cost\n    \n    # Find minimum cost to visit all vertices\n    full_mask = (1 << N) - 1\n    result = INF\n    \n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        result = min(result, dp[full_mask][i])\n    \n    if result == INF:\n        print(\"No\")\n    else:\n        print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
