    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Read the grid\n    grid = []\n    for i in range(2, 2 + H):\n        grid.append(list(data[i]))\n    \n    # Create a working copy (we'll use '.' to mark removed cookies)\n    cookies = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    while True:\n        marked = set()\n        \n        # Step 1: Check rows\n        for i in range(H):\n            # Get remaining cookies in this row\n            row_cookies = [(i, j, cookies[i][j]) for j in range(W) if cookies[i][j] != '.']\n            if len(row_cookies) >= 2:\n                # Check if all remaining cookies in this row have the same color\n                colors = [cookie[2] for cookie in row_cookies]\n                if all(c == colors[0] for c in colors):\n                    # Mark all cookies in this row\n                    for (r, c, _) in row_cookies:\n                        marked.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Step 2: Check columns\n        for j in range(W):\n            # Get remaining cookies in this column\n            col_cookies = [(i, j, cookies[i][j]) for i in range(H) if cookies[i][j] != '.']\n            if len(col_cookies) >= 2:\n                # Check if all remaining cookies in this column have the same color\n                colors = [cookie[2] for cookie in col_cookies]\n                if all(c == colors[0] for c in colors):\n                    # Mark all cookies in this column\n                    for (r, c, _) in col_cookies:\n                        marked.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Step 3: If no cookies are marked, terminate\n        if not marked:\n            break\n            \n        # Remove all marked cookies\n        for (i, j) in marked:\n            cookies[i][j] = '.'\n    \n    # Count remaining cookies\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if cookies[i][j] != '.':\n                count += 1\n    \n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
