      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read grid dimensions\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Read grid\n    grid = []\n    index = 2\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = data[index]\n        index += 1\n        grid.append(row)\n    \n    # Find start and goal positions\n    start = None\n    goal = None\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == 'S':\n                start = (i, j)\n            elif grid[i][j] == 'T':\n                goal = (i, j)\n    \n    # Read number of medicines\n    N = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    \n    # Read medicines\n    medicines = {}\n    for _ in range(N):\n        r = int(data[index]) - 1  # Convert to 0-indexed\n        c = int(data[index + 1]) - 1  # Convert to 0-indexed\n        e = int(data[index + 2])\n        medicines[(r, c)] = e\n        index += 3\n    \n    # BFS with state (row, col, energy)\n    # We'll use a 3D visited array: visited[row][col][energy]\n    # But since energy can be up to H*W (max 40000), we need to optimize\n    # Instead, we can use visited[row][col] = max_energy_reached_at_this_cell\n    \n    max_energy = H * W\n    # For each cell, track the maximum energy we've had when visiting it\n    max_energy_at_cell = {}\n    \n    queue = deque()\n    # Start at S with 0 energy\n    queue.append((start[0], start[1], 0))\n    max_energy_at_cell[(start[0], start[1])] = 0\n    \n    # Directions: up, down, left, right\n    directions = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c, energy = queue.popleft()\n        \n        # If we reached the goal\n        if (r, c) == goal:\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n            \n        # If current energy state is worse than previously explored, skip\n        if energy < max_energy_at_cell.get((r, c), -1):\n            continue\n            \n        # Use medicine if available at current cell\n        if (r, c) in medicines:\n            new_energy = medicines[(r, c)]\n            if new_energy > energy:\n                # Update energy after using medicine\n                if (r, c) not in max_energy_at_cell or new_energy > max_energy_at_cell[(r, c)]:\n                    max_energy_at_cell[(r, c)] = new_energy\n                    queue.append((r, c, new_energy))\n                continue  # After using medicine, we stay in the same cell with new energy\n        \n        # Move to adjacent cells\n        if energy > 0:  # Can only move if we have energy\n            for dr, dc in directions:\n                nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and grid[nr][nc] != '#':\n                    new_energy = energy - 1\n                    # Check if we've reached this cell with higher energy before\n                    state_key = (nr, nc)\n                    if state_key not in max_energy_at_cell or new_energy > max_energy_at_cell[state_key]:\n                        max_energy_at_cell[state_key] = new_energy\n                        queue.append((nr, nc, new_energy))\n    \n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
