      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minLength(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove all occurrences of \"AB\" or \"CD\" from the string until no more can be removed.\n    Return the minimum possible length of the resulting string.\n    \n    Args:\n        s (str): Input string consisting of uppercase English letters\n        \n    Returns:\n        int: Minimum possible length after removing all possible \"AB\" and \"CD\" substrings\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a stack to efficiently handle the removals\n    stack = []\n    \n    for char in s:\n        # Check if adding current character forms \"AB\" or \"CD\" with the top of stack\n        if stack:\n            # Check for \"AB\" (A in stack, B current)\n            if stack[-1] == 'A' and char == 'B':\n                stack.pop()  # Remove 'A', don't add 'B'\n                continue\n            # Check for \"CD\" (C in stack, D current)\n            elif stack[-1] == 'C' and char == 'D':\n                stack.pop()  # Remove 'C', don't add 'D'\n                continue\n        \n        # If no removal, add current character to stack\n        stack.append(char)\n    \n    return len(stack)\n```",
