      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    q = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Store adjacency list for each vertex\n    adj = [set() for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Track isolated vertices (not connected to any other)\n    isolated_count = n  # Initially all vertices are isolated\n    \n    index = 2\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(q):\n        query_type = int(data[index])\n        \n        if query_type == 1:  # Add edge between u and v\n            u = int(data[index + 1])\n            v = int(data[index + 2])\n            index += 3\n            \n            # If u was isolated, it's no longer isolated\n            if len(adj[u]) == 0:\n                isolated_count -= 1\n            \n            # If v was isolated, it's no longer isolated\n            if len(adj[v]) == 0:\n                isolated_count -= 1\n            \n            # Add edge\n            adj[u].add(v)\n            adj[v].add(u)\n            \n        else:  # query_type == 2, remove all edges from vertex v\n            v = int(data[index + 1])\n            index += 2\n            \n            # If v had neighbors, it will become isolated after removal\n            if len(adj[v]) > 0:\n                # Each neighbor loses connection to v\n                for neighbor in adj[v]:\n                    adj[neighbor].remove(v)\n                    # If neighbor becomes isolated, increment count\n                    if len(adj[neighbor]) == 0:\n                        isolated_count += 1\n                \n                # v becomes isolated\n                isolated_count += 1\n            \n            # Clear all edges from v\n            adj[v].clear()\n        \n        results.append(str(isolated_count))\n    \n    print('\\n'.join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
