      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSpecialSubstring(s):\n    # Dictionary to store frequency of each special substring\n    substring_count = {}\n    \n    # Generate all possible substrings\n    n = len(s)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            substring = s[i:j+1]\n            # Check if the substring is special (all characters are the same)\n            if len(set(substring)) == 1:\n                substring_count[substring] = substring_count.get(substring, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find the longest special substring that occurs at least thrice\n    max_length = -1\n    for substring, count in substring_count.items():\n        if count >= 3:\n            max_length = max(max_length, len(substring))\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
