      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    t = int(input())\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        s = input().strip()\n        \n        # If already abc, no swap needed\n        if s == \"abc\":\n            print(\"YES\")\n            continue\n            \n        # Try all possible swaps (at most one allowed)\n        found = False\n        # Convert string to list for swapping\n        chars = list(s)\n        \n        # Try swapping each pair of positions\n        for i in range(3):\n            for j in range(i + 1, 3):\n                # Swap chars[i] and chars[j]\n                chars[i], chars[j] = chars[j], chars[i]\n                \n                # Check if it becomes \"abc\"\n                if ''.join(chars) == \"abc\":\n                    found = True\n                \n                # Swap back to original\n                chars[i], chars[j] = chars[j], chars[i]\n        \n        if found:\n            print(\"YES\")\n        else:\n            print(\"NO\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
