      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().strip().split('\\n')\n    n = int(lines[0])\n    points = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        x, y = map(int, lines[i].split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    # Precompute distances between all pairs\n    def dist(p1, p2):\n        return math.sqrt((p1[0] - p2[0])**2 + (p1[1] - p2[1])**2)\n    \n    # dp[i] = minimum cost to reach checkpoint i (0-indexed)\n    # The cost includes both travel distance and penalty\n    dp = [float('inf')] * n\n    dp[0] = 0  # Start at checkpoint 1 (index 0)\n    \n    # For each checkpoint, try to reach future checkpoints\n    for i in range(n):\n        if dp[i] == float('inf'):\n            continue\n            \n        # Try to go from checkpoint i to j (j > i)\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Number of skipped checkpoints between i and j\n            skipped = j - i - 1\n            \n            # Penalty: 0 if no skips, 2^(C-1) if C > 0\n            penalty = 0 if skipped == 0 else (1 << (skipped - 1))  # 2^(skipped-1)\n            \n            # Distance from i to j\n            distance = dist(points[i], points[j])\n            \n            # Total additional cost\n            total_cost = distance + penalty\n            \n            # Update dp[j]\n            dp[j] = min(dp[j], dp[i] + total_cost)\n    \n    # The answer is the minimum cost to reach the last checkpoint\n    print(f\"{dp[n-1]:.20f}\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
