      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minProcessingTime(processorTime, tasks):\n    # Sort processorTime in ascending order (earlier available processors first)\n    processorTime.sort()\n    \n    # Sort tasks in descending order (longest tasks first)\n    tasks.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    max_completion_time = 0\n    \n    # Each processor handles 4 tasks\n    for i in range(len(processorTime)):\n        # Get the 4 longest remaining tasks for this processor\n        # Tasks are sorted in descending order, so take tasks[i*4 : i*4 + 4]\n        processor_start_time = processorTime[i]\n        \n        # The completion time for this processor is its start time plus the longest task it handles\n        # Since tasks are sorted descending, the first task in its batch is the longest\n        completion_time = processor_start_time + tasks[i * 4]\n        \n        max_completion_time = max(max_completion_time, completion_time)\n    \n    return max_completion_time\n```",
