      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef stringIndices(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    def get_suffix_score(word, query):\n        # Find the longest common suffix\n        min_len = min(len(word), len(query))\n        common_suffix_len = 0\n        for i in range(1, min_len + 1):\n            if word[-i] == query[-i]:\n                common_suffix_len = i\n            else:\n                break\n        return common_suffix_len\n    \n    ans = []\n    \n    # Preprocess wordsContainer to avoid repeated calculations\n    # For each query, we need to find the best match\n    for query in wordsQuery:\n        best_index = 0\n        best_suffix_len = get_suffix_score(wordsContainer[0], query)\n        best_length = len(wordsContainer[0])\n        \n        for i in range(1, len(wordsContainer)):\n            word = wordsContainer[i]\n            suffix_len = get_suffix_score(word, query)\n            \n            # Check if this word is a better candidate\n            if suffix_len > best_suffix_len:\n                best_suffix_len = suffix_len\n                best_length = len(word)\n                best_index = i\n            elif suffix_len == best_suffix_len:\n                # Same suffix length, check for shorter length\n                if len(word) < best_length:\n                    best_length = len(word)\n                    best_index = i\n                # If same length, the one with earlier index wins (we don't need to update)\n        \n        ans.append(best_index)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
