      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    # Read input\n    N, M = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        grid.append(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    \n    # Define the Tak Code pattern\n    # A 9x9 Tak Code has:\n    # - 3x3 black square at top-left (rows 0-2, cols 0-2)\n    # - 3x3 black square at bottom-right (rows 6-8, cols 6-8)\n    # - All cells adjacent to these two 3x3 regions must be white\n    # Adjacent cells include all 8 directions\n    \n    def is_tak_code_region(top_row, left_col):\n        # Check if the 9x9 region starting at (top_row, left_col) is a valid Tak Code\n        \n        # Check top-left 3x3: all must be black (#)\n        for i in range(3):\n            for j in range(3):\n                if grid[top_row + i][left_col + j] != '#':\n                    return False\n        \n        # Check bottom-right 3x3: all must be black (#)\n        for i in range(6, 9):\n            for j in range(6, 9):\n                if grid[top_row + i][left_col + j] != '#':\n                    return False\n        \n        # Check cells adjacent to top-left 3x3 region (must be white)\n        # Adjacent cells are: row -1 to 3, col -1 to 3, excluding the 3x3 itself\n        for i in range(-1, 4):\n            for j in range(-1, 4):\n                # Skip if it's part of the 3x3 black region\n                if 0 <= i <= 2 and 0 <= j <= 2:\n                    continue\n                # Skip if out of the 9x9 region\n                if i < 0 or i >= 9 or j < 0 or j >= 9:\n                    continue\n                # The cell should be white\n                if grid[top_row + i][left_col + j] != '.':\n                    return False\n        \n        # Check cells adjacent to bottom-right 3x3 region (must be white)\n        # Adjacent cells are: row 5 to 9, col 5 to 9, excluding the 3x3 itself\n        for i in range(5, 10):\n            for j in range(5, 10):\n                # Skip if it's part of the 3x3 black region\n                if 6 <= i <= 8 and 6 <= j <= 8:\n                    continue\n                # Skip if out of the 9x9 region\n                if i < 0 or i >= 9 or j < 0 or j >= 9:\n                    continue\n                # The cell should be white\n                if grid[top_row + i][left_col + j] != '.':\n                    return False\n        \n        return True\n    \n    # Find all valid 9x9 regions\n    results = []\n    for i in range(N - 8):  # top row can be from 0 to N-9\n        for j in range(M - 8):  # left column can be from 0 to M-9\n            if is_tak_code_region(i, j):\n                results.append((i + 1, j + 1))  # 1-indexed\n    \n    # Output results (already in lexicographical order due to loop order)\n    for i, j in results:\n        print(i, j)\n\nsolve()\n```",
