      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    S = input().strip()\n    T = input().strip()\n    \n    # Check first method: subsequence of length 3\n    def can_form_subsequence(target, source):\n        j = 0\n        for i in range(len(source)):\n            if j < len(target) and source[i].upper() == target[j]:\n                j += 1\n        return j == len(target)\n    \n    # Method 1: Check if T can be formed by a subsequence of length 3\n    if can_form_subsequence(T, S):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n    \n    # Method 2: Check if first 2 chars of T can be formed, and T ends with X\n    if T[2] == 'X':\n        if can_form_subsequence(T[:2], S):\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n    \n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
