      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    bases = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        w, x = map(int, input().split())\n        bases.append((w, x))\n    \n    max_participants = 0\n    \n    # Try all possible meeting start times in UTC (0-23, since meeting is 1 hour)\n    for utc_start in range(24):\n        participants = 0\n        for w, x in bases:\n            # Local start time at this base\n            local_start = (utc_start + x) % 24\n            # Local end time (one hour meeting)\n            local_end = (local_start + 1) % 24\n            \n            # Check if the entire meeting (start to end) is within 9-18 (9:00-18:00)\n            # Note: 18:00 is the end of working hours, so meeting must end by 18:00\n            # This means local_end <= 18 and local_start >= 9\n            if local_start >= 9 and local_end <= 18:\n                participants += w\n        \n        max_participants = max(max_participants, participants)\n    \n    print(max_participants)\n\nsolve()\n```",
