    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_477",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given an integer array coins representing coins of different denominations and an integer k.\nYou have an infinite number of coins of each denomination. However, you are not allowed to combine coins of different denominations.\nReturn the k^th smallest amount that can be made using these coins.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: coins = [3,6,9], k = 3\nOutput:  9\nExplanation: The given coins can make the following amounts:\nCoin 3 produces multiples of 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, etc.\nCoin 6 produces multiples of 6: 6, 12, 18, 24, etc.\nCoin 9 produces multiples of 9: 9, 18, 27, 36, etc.\nAll of the coins combined produce: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, etc.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: coins = [5,2], k = 7\nOutput: 12 \nExplanation: The given coins can make the following amounts:\nCoin 5 produces multiples of 5: 5, 10, 15, 20, etc.\nCoin 2 produces multiples of 2: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, etc.\nAll of the coins combined produce: 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, etc.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= coins.length <= 15\n1 <= coins[i] <= 25\n1 <= k <= 2 * 10^9\ncoins contains pairwise distinct integers.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findKthSmallestAmount(coins, k):\n    import heapq\n    \n    # Sort coins to process smaller denominations first\n    coins.sort()\n    \n    # Use a min heap to generate amounts in increasing order\n    heap = []\n    # Use a set to avoid duplicates\n    seen = set()\n    \n    # Initialize heap with the first multiple of each coin\n    for coin in coins:\n        heapq.heappush(heap, coin)\n        seen.add(coin)\n    \n    # Extract k smallest amounts\n    for _ in range(k):\n        # Get the smallest amount\n        current = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        \n        # If this is the kth element, return it\n        if _ == k - 1:\n            return current\n        \n        # Add the next multiple of the same denomination\n        # Find which coin denomination produced this amount\n        for coin in coins:\n            if current % coin == 0:\n                next_amount = current + coin\n                if next_amount not in seen:\n                    seen.add(next_amount)\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, next_amount)\n    \n    return -1\n```",
