    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Read grid A\n    A = []\n    index = 2\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = list(map(int, data[index:index+W]))\n        A.append(row)\n        index += W\n    \n    # Read grid B\n    B = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = list(map(int, data[index:index+W]))\n        B.append(row)\n        index += W\n    \n    # If A is already equal to B\n    if A == B:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # Use BFS to find minimum number of operations\n    visited = set()\n    queue = deque()\n    \n    # Convert grid to tuple for hashing\n    def grid_to_tuple(grid):\n        return tuple(tuple(row) for row in grid)\n    \n    start = grid_to_tuple(A)\n    target = grid_to_tuple(B)\n    \n    visited.add(start)\n    queue.append((start, 0))\n    \n    while queue:\n        current_grid_tuple, steps = queue.popleft()\n        current_grid = [list(row) for row in current_grid_tuple]\n        \n        # Try all possible row swaps (i and i+1)\n        for i in range(H - 1):\n            new_grid = [row[:] for row in current_grid]  # Copy grid\n            new_grid[i], new_grid[i+1] = new_grid[i+1], new_grid[i]  # Swap rows\n            new_tuple = grid_to_tuple(new_grid)\n            \n            if new_tuple == target:\n                print(steps + 1)\n                return\n                \n            if new_tuple not in visited:\n                visited.add(new_tuple)\n                queue.append((new_tuple, steps + 1))\n        \n        # Try all possible column swaps (j and j+1)\n        for j in range(W - 1):\n            new_grid = [row[:] for row in current_grid]  # Copy grid\n            # Swap column j and j+1 for each row\n            for i in range(H):\n                new_grid[i][j], new_grid[i][j+1] = new_grid[i][j+1], new_grid[i][j]\n            new_tuple = grid_to_tuple(new_grid)\n            \n            if new_tuple == target:\n                print(steps + 1)\n                return\n                \n            if new_tuple not in visited:\n                visited.add(new_tuple)\n                queue.append((new_tuple, steps + 1))\n    \n    # If we've exhausted all possibilities and haven't reached B\n    print(-1)\n\nsolve()\n```",
