      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse initial input\n    n = int(data[0])\n    q = int(data[1])\n    s = data[2]\n    \n    # Convert string to list for easier manipulation\n    s_list = list(s)\n    index = 3\n    \n    output_lines = []\n    \n    for _ in range(q):\n        query_type = int(data[index])\n        l = int(data[index + 1])\n        r = int(data[index + 2])\n        index += 3\n        \n        if query_type == 1:\n            # Flip characters from position L to R (1-indexed)\n            for i in range(l - 1, r):\n                if s_list[i] == '0':\n                    s_list[i] = '1'\n                else:\n                    s_list[i] = '0'\n        else:  # query_type == 2\n            # Extract substring from L to R (1-indexed)\n            substring = s_list[l - 1:r]\n            \n            # Check if it's a good string (no two consecutive characters are the same)\n            is_good = True\n            for i in range(len(substring) - 1):\n                if substring[i] == substring[i + 1]:\n                    is_good = False\n                    break\n            \n            output_lines.append(\"Yes\" if is_good else \"No\")\n    \n    # Print all outputs\n    for line in output_lines:\n        print(line)\n\nsolve()\n```",
