      "generated_answer": "We are given:\n\n- N bus stops between Takahashi's house and Aoki's house.\n- He walks from home to stop 1 in X time.\n- From stop i to i+1, a bus departs every P_i units of time (at multiples of P_i), and takes T_i time.\n- He walks from stop N to Aoki’s house in Y time.\n- Queries: for each departure time q_i from home, compute the earliest arrival time at Aoki’s house.\n\nWe need to simulate the journey:\n\n1. Start at time `q_i`, arrive at stop 1 at `q_i + X`.\n2. For each bus stop i from 1 to N-1:\n   - Wait until the next (or current) bus that departs at a multiple of P_i and is ≥ current time.\n   - The next departure time is: `ceil(current_time / P_i) * P_i`\n   - Then add T_i to get to stop i+1.\n3. Finally, add Y to get to Aoki's house.\n\nSince `P_i` is at most 8, we don't have to worry about performance in computing the ceiling division.\n\nWe'll process Q queries.\n\nLet’s write the code accordingly.\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    N = int(data[0]); X = int(data[1]); Y = int(data[2])\n    buses = []\n    index = 3\n    for i in range(N-1):\n        P = int(data[index]); T = int(data[index+1]); index += 2\n        buses.append((P, T))\n    \n    Q = int(data[index]); index += 1\n    queries = [int(data[index + i]) for i in range(Q)]\n    \n    results = []\n    for q in queries:\n        time = q + X  # arrival at bus stop 1\n        \n        # Travel from stop 1 to stop N via buses\n        for P, T in buses:\n            # Wait for next bus: smallest multiple of P >= time\n            if time % P == 0:\n                departure_time = time\n            else:\n                departure_time = ((time // P) + 1) * P\n            time = departure_time + T  # arrive at next stop\n        \n        # Walk from stop N to Aoki's house\n        time += Y\n        results.append(str(time))\n    \n    print(\"\\n\".join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
