    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestCommonPrefix(arr1, arr2):\n    # Convert all numbers to strings and store all possible prefixes of arr1\n    prefixes = set()\n    \n    for num in arr1:\n        str_num = str(num)\n        # Add all prefixes of this number\n        for i in range(1, len(str_num) + 1):\n            prefixes.add(str_num[:i])\n    \n    max_length = 0\n    \n    # For each number in arr2, check all its prefixes\n    for num in arr2:\n        str_num = str(num)\n        # Check each prefix of this number from longest to shortest\n        for i in range(len(str_num), 0, -1):\n            prefix = str_num[:i]\n            if prefix in prefixes:\n                max_length = max(max_length, len(prefix))\n                break  # Found the longest prefix for this number, no need to check shorter ones\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
