    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxPalindromes(words):\n    # Count frequency of each character\n    char_count = {}\n    for word in words:\n        for char in word:\n            char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Sort words by length in ascending order to maximize palindrome count\n    words_sorted = sorted(words, key=len)\n    \n    palindrome_count = 0\n    remaining_chars = char_count.copy()\n    \n    for word in words_sorted:\n        word_len = len(word)\n        # Check if we can form a palindrome of this length\n        odd_count = 0  # Count of characters that need to appear odd number of times\n        temp_chars = remaining_chars.copy()\n        \n        # For a palindrome, at most one character can have odd frequency\n        # We need to check if we have enough characters to form a palindrome of this length\n        \n        # Calculate how many characters we need with odd frequency\n        # For even length: all characters must have even frequency\n        # For odd length: exactly one character must have odd frequency\n        needed_odd = 1 if word_len % 2 == 1 else 0\n        \n        # Count how many characters currently have odd frequency\n        current_odd = sum(1 for count in temp_chars.values() if count % 2 == 1)\n        \n        # Check if we can form a palindrome\n        if current_odd <= needed_odd:\n            # We have enough odd-frequency characters\n            # Check if total available characters are sufficient\n            total_available = sum(temp_chars.values())\n            if total_available >= word_len:\n                # We can form a palindrome\n                palindrome_count += 1\n                \n                # Remove the used characters (just conceptually use word_len characters)\n                # Greedily use characters to form the palindrome\n                chars_to_use = word_len\n                for char in temp_chars:\n                    if chars_to_use == 0:\n                        break\n                    use = min(temp_chars[char], chars_to_use)\n                    temp_chars[char] -= use\n                    chars_to_use -= use\n                \n                # Update remaining characters\n                remaining_chars = temp_chars\n        else:\n            # We have too many odd-frequency characters\n            # We need to check if we can reduce odd counts by using characters\n            # The minimum characters needed to fix the odd counts\n            excess_odd = current_odd - needed_odd\n            # We need to use at least excess_odd characters to fix the odd counts\n            # plus the word length\n            if sum(temp_chars.values()) >= word_len:\n                # We can potentially fix it\n                # Use a greedy approach: try to form the palindrome\n                palindrome_count += 1\n                \n                # Use word_len characters to form palindrome\n                chars_to_use = word_len\n                temp_chars_copy = temp_chars.copy()\n                for char in temp_chars_copy:\n                    if chars_to_use == 0:\n                        break\n                    use = min(temp_chars[char], chars_to_use)\n                    temp_chars[char] -= use\n                    chars_to_use -= use\n                \n                remaining_chars = temp_chars\n    \n    return palindrome_count\n```",
