    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    S = data[2]\n    T = data[3]\n    \n    # We start with a string X of N '#' characters\n    # We want to check if we can transform X to S using the operation\n    # Operation: choose M consecutive characters and replace them with T\n    \n    # Since M is at most 5, we can use dynamic programming or greedy approach\n    # We'll use a greedy approach from left to right\n    \n    # Create an array to track which positions can be covered\n    # We can think of this as: can we make the prefix of S up to position i?\n    \n    # Instead, let's use a different approach:\n    # We'll simulate from left to right, and whenever we see that we can place T\n    # to match a part of S, we mark that we can reach that state.\n    \n    # But a simpler approach: work backwards or use the fact that we can overlap operations\n    # Since we can perform operations any number of times, we need to check if S can be\n    # constructed by overlapping copies of T.\n    \n    # Key insight: We can use dynamic programming where dp[i] = True if we can match S[0:i]\n    dp = [False] * (N + 1)\n    dp[0] = True  # Empty prefix is always possible\n    \n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        # Check if we can reach position i\n        for j in range(max(0, i - M), i):\n            if dp[j] and i - j == M:\n                # Check if S[j:i] matches T\n                if S[j:i] == T:\n                    dp[i] = True\n                    break\n            # We can also consider that we might have built up to j and then placed T\n            # starting at position j such that it ends at position i\n            if j + M <= N and dp[j]:\n                if S[j:j + M] == T:\n                    dp[j + M] = True\n    \n    # Recompute with a clearer DP approach\n    dp = [False] * (N + 1)\n    dp[0] = True\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        if not dp[i]:\n            continue\n        # From position i, we can place T starting at position i\n        if i + M <= N and S[i:i + M] == T:\n            dp[i + M] = True\n    \n    if dp[N]:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
