    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nVanya and Vova are playing a game. Players are given an integer $n$. On their turn, the player can add $1$ to the current integer or subtract $1$. The players take turns; Vanya starts. If after Vanya's move the integer is divisible by $3$, then he wins. If $10$ moves have passed and Vanya has not won, then Vova wins.\n\nWrite a program that, based on the integer $n$, determines who will win if both players play optimally.\n\nInput\n\nThe first line contains the integer $t$ ($1 \\leq t \\leq 100$) — the number of test cases.\n\nThe single line of each test case contains the integer $n$ ($1 \\leq n \\leq 1000$).\n\nOutput\n\nFor each test case, print \"First\" without quotes if Vanya wins, and \"Second\" without quotes if Vova wins.Sample Input 1:\n6\n\n1\n\n3\n\n5\n\n100\n\n999\n\n1000\n\n\n\nSample Output 1:\n\nFirst\nSecond\nFirst\nFirst\nSecond\nFirst\n",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    t = int(input())\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input())\n        \n        # Vanya moves first and wins immediately if after his move n is divisible by 3\n        # So Vanya will win if he can make (n ± 1) divisible by 3\n        \n        # Vanya can choose to do n+1 or n-1\n        # He wins if either (n+1) % 3 == 0 or (n-1) % 3 == 0\n        \n        # (n+1) % 3 == 0  => n % 3 == 2\n        # (n-1) % 3 == 0  => n % 3 == 1\n        # So Vanya wins if n % 3 != 0\n        \n        # If n % 3 == 0, then neither n+1 nor n-1 is divisible by 3\n        # In this case, Vova can always prevent Vanya from winning in subsequent moves?\n        \n        # Let's analyze:\n        # If n % 3 == 0:\n        #   Vanya moves to either n+1 (≡ 1 mod 3) or n-1 (≡ 2 mod 3)\n        #   Then Vova can move to make it ≡ 0 mod 3 again:\n        #     If Vanya goes to n+1 (≡ 1), Vova goes to n (≡ 0)\n        #     If Vanya goes to n-1 (≡ 2), Vova goes to n (≡ 0)\n        #   So Vova can always restore n % 3 == 0 after his move\n        #   This means Vanya can never win, since his moves will always be from a multiple of 3\n        #   Therefore, after 10 moves, Vova wins\n        \n        # If n % 3 != 0:\n        #   Vanya can immediately win by choosing the right move:\n        #     If n % 3 == 1, choose n-1 → divisible by 3\n        #     If n % 3 == 2, choose n+1 → divisible by 3\n        \n        if n % 3 == 0:\n            print(\"Second\")\n        else:\n            print(\"First\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
