      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    \n    # Store each person's bets and the count of their bets\n    people_bets = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        c = int(input())\n        bets = list(map(int, input().split()))\n        people_bets.append((c, set(bets)))\n    \n    X = int(input())\n    \n    # Find all people who bet on X and their bet counts\n    people_who_bet_on_x = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        if X in people_bets[i][1]:\n            people_who_bet_on_x.append((i + 1, people_bets[i][0]))  # (person_number, number_of_bets)\n    \n    # If no one bet on X, output 0\n    if not people_who_bet_on_x:\n        print(0)\n        print()\n        return\n    \n    # Find the minimum number of bets among those who bet on X\n    min_bets = min(count for person, count in people_who_bet_on_x)\n    \n    # Find all people who bet on X and have the minimum number of bets\n    result = [person for person, count in people_who_bet_on_x if count == min_bets]\n    result.sort()  # Should already be in order, but just to be safe\n    \n    # Output the result\n    print(len(result))\n    if result:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, result)))\n    else:\n        print()\n\nsolve()\n```",
