    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum cost to convert source to target by changing characters. This is essentially a shortest path problem where each character is a node and each transformation is an edge with a cost.\n\nKey insights:\n1. I need to find the minimum cost to transform each character in source to the corresponding character in target\n2. Some transformations might require multiple steps (e.g., 'a' → 'c' → 'b')\n3. I should use Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find the shortest path between all pairs of characters\n4. If any character in source cannot be transformed to the corresponding character in target, return -1\n\nHere's my approach:\n1. Create a distance matrix for all 26 lowercase letters\n2. Initialize direct transformation costs from the given arrays\n3. Use Floyd-Warshall to find minimum cost between all pairs\n4. Calculate total cost by summing up the minimum cost for each position\n\n```python\ndef minimumCost(source, target, original, changed, cost):\n    # Initialize distance matrix with infinity\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(26)]\n    \n    # Distance from a character to itself is 0\n    for i in range(26):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n    \n    # Add direct transformation costs\n    for i in range(len(original)):\n        orig_idx = ord(original[i]) - ord('a')\n        chng_idx = ord(changed[i]) - ord('a')\n        # Keep the minimum cost if there are duplicate transformations\n        dist[orig_idx][chng_idx] = min(dist[orig_idx][chng_idx], cost[i])\n    \n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find shortest paths between all pairs\n    for k in range(26):\n        for i in range(26):\n            for j in range(26):\n                if dist[i][k] != INF and dist[k][j] != INF:\n                    dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])\n    \n    # Calculate total minimum cost\n    total_cost = 0\n    n = len(source)\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        if source[i] == target[i]:\n            continue\n            \n        src_idx = ord(source[i]) - ord('a')\n        tgt_idx = ord(target[i]) - ord('a')\n        \n        # If no path exists from source[i] to target[i]\n        if dist[src_idx][tgt_idx] == INF:\n            return -1\n            \n        total_cost += dist[src_idx][tgt_idx]\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
