    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a string word and an integer k.\nA substring s of word is complete if:\n\nEach character in s occurs exactly k times.\nThe difference between two adjacent characters is at most 2. That is, for any two adjacent characters c1 and c2 in s, the absolute difference in their positions in the alphabet is at most 2.\n\nReturn the number of complete substrings of word.\nA substring is a non-empty contiguous sequence of characters in a string.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: word = \"igigee\", k = 2\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: The complete substrings where each character appears exactly twice and the difference between adjacent characters is at most 2 are: igigee, igigee, igigee.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: word = \"aaabbbccc\", k = 3\nOutput: 6\nExplanation: The complete substrings where each character appears exactly three times and the difference between adjacent characters is at most 2 are: aaabbbccc, aaabbbccc, aaabbbccc, aaabbbccc, aaabbbccc, aaabbbccc.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= word.length <= 10^5\nword consists only of lowercase English letters.\n1 <= k <= word.length",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to:\n\n1. Find substrings where each character appears exactly k times\n2. The difference between adjacent characters in the alphabet is at most 2\n3. Count how many such \"complete\" substrings exist\n\nLet me analyze the examples:\n- Example 1: \"igigee\", k=2. Characters: i(9), g(7), e(5). Differences: |9-7|=2, |7-9|=2, |9-7|=2, |7-5|=2, |5-5|=0 - all ≤ 2.\n- Example 2: \"aaabbbccc\", k=3. All adjacent characters are the same, so difference is 0.\n\nKey insights:\n1. For a substring to have each character appear exactly k times, if there are `u` unique characters, the substring length must be `u * k`\n2. I can iterate through possible numbers of unique characters (1 to 26) and for each, check substrings of length `u * k`\n3. For each potential substring, verify:\n   - All adjacent character differences ≤ 2\n   - Each character in the substring appears exactly k times\n\n```python\ndef countCompleteSubstrings(word, k):\n    def is_valid_adjacent(s):\n        for i in range(len(s) - 1):\n            if abs(ord(s[i]) - ord(s[i + 1])) > 2:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    def is_complete(substring, k):\n        if not is_valid_adjacent(substring):\n            return False\n        \n        char_count = {}\n        for char in substring:\n            char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n        \n        for count in char_count.values():\n            if count != k:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    n = len(word)\n    count = 0\n    \n    # Try all possible substring lengths that could be complete\n    # Length must be u * k where u is number of unique characters (1 to 26)\n    for unique_count in range(1, 27):\n        length = unique_count * k\n        if length > n:\n            break\n            \n        # Check all substrings of this length\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            substring = word[i:i + length]\n            if is_complete(substring, k):\n                count += 1\n    \n    return count\n```",
