      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumNumberOfStringPairs(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the maximum number of pairs that can be formed from the array words,\n    where a pair consists of two strings where one is the reverse of the other.\n    \n    Args:\n        words: List of distinct strings of length 2\n        \n    Returns:\n        Maximum number of pairs that can be formed\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a set to keep track of strings we've seen\n    seen = set()\n    pairs = 0\n    \n    for word in words:\n        # Create the reversed version of the current word\n        reversed_word = word[::-1]\n        \n        # If the reversed word is already in our set, we found a pair\n        if reversed_word in seen:\n            pairs += 1\n            # Remove the reversed word since it's now paired\n            seen.remove(reversed_word)\n        else:\n            # Add the current word to our set\n            seen.add(word)\n    \n    return pairs\n```",
