      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N, S, M, L = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # We need at least N eggs\n    # We can buy any number of packs of 6, 8, or 12 eggs\n    \n    # Since N <= 100, we can use brute force to try all reasonable combinations\n    # Maximum packs needed: ceil(N/6) for 6-egg packs, etc.\n    # But we might want to buy more than N eggs, so we need to consider reasonable upper bounds\n    \n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    \n    # Upper bounds for each type of pack\n    # We won't need more than N//6 + 2 of 6-egg packs, etc.\n    # But to be safe, we can use N//min(6,8,12) + 5 = N//6 + 5\n    max_s = (N // 6) + 10  # packs of 6\n    max_m = (N // 8) + 10  # packs of 8\n    max_l = (N // 12) + 10  # packs of 12\n    \n    # Try all combinations within reasonable bounds\n    for s in range(max_s + 1):\n        for m in range(max_m + 1):\n            for l in range(max_l + 1):\n                total_eggs = 6 * s + 8 * m + 12 * l\n                if total_eggs >= N:\n                    total_cost = s * S + m * M + l * L\n                    min_cost = min(min_cost, total_cost)\n    \n    print(min_cost)\n\nsolve()\n```",
