\n00110\r\n10100",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        row = list(input().strip())\n        grid.append([int(x) for x in row])\n    \n    # If N is 1, no shifting needed (though constraint says N >= 2)\n    if N == 1:\n        for row in grid:\n            print(''.join(map(str, row)))\n        return\n    \n    # Extract the outer ring in clockwise order\n    outer = []\n    \n    # Top row (left to right): (1,1) to (1,N)\n    for j in range(N):\n        outer.append((0, j, grid[0][j]))\n    \n    # Right column (top to bottom, excluding top-right corner): (2,N) to (N,N)\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        outer.append((i, N-1, grid[i][N-1]))\n    \n    # Bottom row (right to left, excluding bottom-right corner): (N,N-1) to (N,1)\n    for j in range(N-2, -1, -1):\n        outer.append((N-1, j, grid[N-1][j]))\n    \n    # Left column (bottom to top, excluding bottom-left and top-left corners): (N-1,1) to (2,1)\n    for i in range(N-2, 0, -1):\n        outer.append((i, 0, grid[i][0]))\n    \n    # Shift clockwise by one position\n    # This means each element moves to the next position in the outer list\n    # The last element wraps around to the first position\n    \n    # Create new values after shift\n    shifted_values = [outer[-1][2]]  # Last element goes to first position\n    for i in range(len(outer) - 1):\n        shifted_values.append(outer[i][2])\n    \n    # Place the shifted values back to the grid\n    for i, (row, col, _) in enumerate(outer):\n        grid[row][col] = shifted_values[i]\n    \n    # Print the result\n    for row in grid:\n        print(''.join(map(str, row)))\n\nsolve()\n```",
