    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumBeautifulSubstrings(s):\n    if s[0] == '0':\n        return -1\n    \n    # Generate all powers of 5 that can fit in a 15-bit binary string\n    powers_of_5 = []\n    power = 1\n    while power < 2**15:\n        powers_of_5.append(bin(power)[2:])  # Convert to binary string without '0b' prefix\n        power *= 5\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum number of beautiful substrings for s[:i]\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0  # Empty string requires 0 substrings\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):\n            # Check if s[j:i] is a beautiful substring\n            substring = s[j:i]\n            # Check for leading zeros (except for \"0\" itself, but \"0\" isn't a power of 5)\n            if substring[0] == '0':\n                continue\n            if substring in powers_of_5 and dp[j] != float('inf'):\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n    \n    return dp[n] if dp[n] != float('inf') else -1\n```",
