    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfPowerfulInt(start, finish, limit, s):\n    def count_powerful(num_str):\n        n = len(num_str)\n        s_len = len(s)\n        \n        # If s is longer than num_str, no powerful integer <= num_str\n        if s_len > n:\n            return 0\n        \n        # Check if the suffix part exceeds the limit\n        for i in range(s_len):\n            if int(s[i]) > limit:\n                return 0\n        \n        # Check if the suffix constraint can be satisfied\n        suffix_start = n - s_len\n        for i in range(s_len):\n            if int(num_str[suffix_start + i]) < int(s[i]):\n                # We can form numbers with the given suffix that are <= num_str\n                # by reducing the prefix part\n                break\n            elif int(num_str[suffix_start + i]) > int(s[i]):\n                # We can use the full range for prefix\n                prefix_max = int(num_str[:suffix_start]) if suffix_start > 0 else 0\n                return (prefix_max + 1) if suffix_start == 0 else (min(prefix_max + 1, (limit + 1) ** suffix_start))\n            # if equal, continue to check next digit\n        else:\n            # All suffix digits match, check if prefix is valid\n            prefix_val = int(num_str[:suffix_start]) if suffix_start > 0 else 0\n            return prefix_val + 1\n        \n        # Count numbers with the given suffix and digits <= limit\n        if suffix_start == 0:\n            return 1  # Only one number - the suffix itself\n        \n        # Count all valid prefixes (each digit <= limit)\n        total = 0\n        prefix_str = num_str[:suffix_start]\n        \n        # Calculate how many valid numbers we can form with prefix digits\n        tight = True\n        for i in range(suffix_start):\n            digit = int(prefix_str[i])\n            if tight:\n                # Count digits from 0 to min(digit, limit)\n                max_digit = min(digit, limit)\n                total = total * (limit + 1) + (max_digit + 1)\n                if digit > limit:\n                    tight = False\n            else:\n                total = total * (limit + 1) + (limit + 1)\n                \n        return total\n    \n    def count_up_to(n):\n        if n < int(s):\n            return 0\n        return count_powerful(str(n))\n    \n    return count_up_to(finish) - count_up_to(start - 1)\n```",
