      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not data: \n        return\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    N, Q = map(int, data[0].split())\n    \n    # Parse string\n    S = data[1].strip()\n    \n    # Precompute prefix sum array for consecutive duplicates\n    # prefix[i] = number of consecutive duplicates from index 0 to i-1 (1-indexed)\n    prefix = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    for i in range(1, N):\n        prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i]\n        if S[i] == S[i - 1]:\n            prefix[i + 1] += 1\n    \n    # Process queries\n    for i in range(2, 2 + Q):\n        line = data[i].split()\n        l = int(line[0])\n        r = int(line[1])\n        \n        # We need to count positions p where l <= p <= r-1 and S[p-1] == S[p]\n        # (converting to 0-indexed)\n        \n        # The consecutive pairs are at positions (1,2), (2,3), ..., (r-1,r)\n        # In 0-indexed, we check positions 0,1,...,r-2\n        # We want pairs starting at positions from l-1 to r-2\n        \n        if r - l < 1:  # length 1, no consecutive pairs possible\n            print(0)\n            continue\n            \n        # Count consecutive duplicates from position l-1 to r-2 (0-indexed)\n        # This is prefix[r] - prefix[l]\n        # prefix[r] counts duplicates up to position r-1 (pair ending at r)\n        # prefix[l] counts duplicates up to position l-1 (pair ending at l)\n        # So we want duplicates from position l to r-1\n        result = prefix[r] - prefix[l]\n        print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
