      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumAddedCoins(coins, target):\n    coins.sort()\n    added = 0\n    current_sum = 0\n    coin_idx = 0\n    \n    for required in range(1, target + 1):\n        # Add existing coins that can contribute to our current range\n        while coin_idx < len(coins) and coins[coin_idx] <= required:\n            current_sum += coins[coin_idx]\n            coin_idx += 1\n            \n        # If we can't form the required value with existing coins\n        if current_sum < required:\n            # Add a coin of value 'required'\n            added += 1\n            current_sum += required\n            # Note: We don't need to track the actual coin value added\n            # because we're just counting how many we need to add\n            \n    return added\n```",
