    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    # Read input\n    N, K = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    P = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split()))\n    \n    # For K = 1, the answer is always 0\n    if K == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # Create position map: value -> index (1-indexed)\n    pos = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(N):\n        pos[P[i]] = i + 1  # Convert to 1-indexed\n    \n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each possible consecutive sequence of K integers\n    # The sequence can be [a, a+1, ..., a+K-1] where a ranges from 1 to N-K+1\n    for a in range(1, N - K + 2):\n        # Get positions of values a, a+1, ..., a+K-1\n        positions = []\n        valid = True\n        \n        for val in range(a, a + K):\n            if pos[val] == 0:  # This shouldn't happen given the constraints\n                valid = False\n                break\n            positions.append(pos[val])\n        \n        if not valid:\n            continue\n            \n        # Sort positions to find the minimum and maximum indices\n        positions.sort()\n        diff = positions[-1] - positions[0]\n        min_diff = min(min_diff, diff)\n    \n    print(min_diff)\n\nsolve()\n```",
