      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    L = int(data[2])\n    \n    # Parse main dish prices\n    a = list(map(int, data[3:3+N]))\n    \n    # Parse side dish prices\n    b = list(map(int, data[3+N:3+N+M]))\n    \n    # Parse forbidden pairs\n    forbidden = set()\n    idx = 3 + N + M\n    for _ in range(L):\n        c = int(data[idx])\n        d = int(data[idx+1])\n        idx += 2\n        forbidden.add((c, d))\n    \n    # Find the most expensive available set meal\n    max_price = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(M):\n            if (i+1, j+1) not in forbidden:\n                price = a[i] + b[j]\n                max_price = max(max_price, price)\n    \n    print(max_price)\n\nsolve()\n```",
