    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getSmallestString(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    if k == 0:\n        return s\n    \n    result = []\n    remaining_k = k\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if remaining_k == 0:\n            result.append(char)\n            continue\n            \n        # Current character's position (0-25)\n        current_pos = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        \n        # Distance to 'a' in cyclic manner\n        # Option 1: go backwards (current_pos steps)\n        # Option 2: go forwards (26 - current_pos steps)\n        dist_to_a = min(current_pos, 26 - current_pos)\n        \n        if dist_to_a <= remaining_k:\n            # We can change this character to 'a'\n            result.append('a')\n            remaining_k -= dist_to_a\n        else:\n            # We can't reach 'a', but we can move towards 'a'\n            # Move as close to 'a' as possible\n            if current_pos <= 13:  # Direct distance is shorter\n                # Move backwards by remaining_k steps\n                new_pos = current_pos - remaining_k\n                result.append(chr(ord('a') + new_pos))\n                remaining_k = 0\n            else:  # Cyclic distance is shorter\n                # We're better off going through the cycle\n                # But since we can't complete the cycle to reach 'a',\n                # we move forward from current position\n                new_pos = current_pos + remaining_k\n                if new_pos >= 26:\n                    new_pos -= 26\n                result.append(chr(ord('a') + new_pos))\n                remaining_k = 0\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```",
