      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input())\n    cups = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        f, s = map(int, input().split())\n        cups.append((f, s))\n    \n    # Group cups by flavor\n    flavor_groups = {}\n    for f, s in cups:\n        if f not in flavor_groups:\n            flavor_groups[f] = []\n        flavor_groups[f].append(s)\n    \n    # Sort deliciousness values in each flavor group in descending order\n    for f in flavor_groups:\n        flavor_groups[f].sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    max_satisfaction = 0\n    \n    # Case 1: Two cups with different flavors\n    # Get the two cups with highest deliciousness from different flavors\n    all_cups_sorted = sorted(cups, key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n    \n    # Find top two cups from different flavors\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            f1, s1 = all_cups_sorted[i]\n            f2, s2 = all_cups_sorted[j]\n            if f1 != f2:\n                satisfaction = s1 + s2\n                max_satisfaction = max(max_satisfaction, satisfaction)\n                break\n        else:\n            continue\n        break\n    \n    # Case 2: Two cups with same flavor\n    # For each flavor with at least 2 cups, try the two most delicious ones\n    for f in flavor_groups:\n        if len(flavor_groups[f]) >= 2:\n            s1, s2 = flavor_groups[f][0], flavor_groups[f][1]\n            satisfaction = s1 + s2 // 2\n            max_satisfaction = max(max_satisfaction, satisfaction)\n    \n    print(max_satisfaction)\n\nsolve()\n```",
