      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef matrixSum(nums):\n    score = 0\n    \n    # Create a copy of the matrix with each row sorted in descending order\n    sorted_rows = []\n    for row in nums:\n        sorted_rows.append(sorted(row, reverse=True))\n    \n    # Get the number of columns (which is the number of operations needed)\n    num_cols = len(nums[0])\n    \n    # For each operation, pick the largest remaining element from each row\n    for col in range(num_cols):\n        max_from_operation = 0\n        for row in sorted_rows:\n            # The largest remaining element is at position 'col'\n            max_from_operation = max(max_from_operation, row[col])\n        \n        # Add the maximum value from this operation to the score\n        score += max_from_operation\n    \n    return score\n```",
