      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef specialPerm(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Precompute which pairs satisfy the condition\n    compatible = [[False] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j and (nums[i] % nums[j] == 0 or nums[j] % nums[i] == 0):\n                compatible[i][j] = True\n    \n    # dp[mask][last] = number of ways to arrange the elements in mask with last element at index 'last'\n    # We'll use memoization with recursion\n    from functools import lru_cache\n    \n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def dp(mask, last_idx):\n        # Count set bits in mask\n        count = bin(mask).count('1')\n        if count == n:\n            return 1\n        \n        result = 0\n        for next_idx in range(n):\n            # If this element is not used and is compatible with the last element\n            if not (mask & (1 << next_idx)) and compatible[last_idx][next_idx]:\n                result = (result + dp(mask | (1 << next_idx), next_idx)) % MOD\n        \n        return result\n    \n    # Try starting with each element\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        total = (total + dp(1 << i, i)) % MOD\n    \n    return total\n```",
