      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum cost to make all characters in a binary string equal (all '0's or all '1's) using two types of operations.\n\nLet me analyze the operations:\n1. Invert from index 0 to i (cost = i + 1)\n2. Invert from index i to n-1 (cost = n - i)\n\nThe key insight is that I need to consider making all characters '0' or all characters '1', and find the minimum cost for each case.\n\nLooking at the pattern, when we have alternating segments, we need to flip at transition points. The optimal strategy involves considering where to apply the operations to minimize total cost.\n\nAfter analyzing the examples and the nature of the operations, I can see that this is a dynamic programming problem where I need to track the state after processing each position.\n\nThe key insight is that I should consider the transitions between consecutive characters. When s[i] != s[i+1], I need to apply operations to make them equal.\n\nFor each transition point, I need to decide whether to use prefix operations, suffix operations, or a combination.\n\n```python\ndef minimumCost(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    \n    # The minimum cost will be the minimum of making all characters '0' or all characters '1'\n    # But we can solve it more directly by considering transition points\n    \n    total_cost = 0\n    \n    # For each position where adjacent characters differ, we need to apply operations\n    # The optimal strategy is to apply the cheaper of prefix or suffix operations at each transition\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if s[i] != s[i + 1]:\n            # We have a transition, we need to flip one side\n            # We can either flip the left part (using prefix operation ending at i) or flip the right part (using suffix operation starting at i+1)\n            # Cost of flipping left part up to i: i + 1\n            # Cost of flipping right part from i+1: n - (i + 1) = n - i - 1\n            total_cost += min(i + 1, n - i - 1)\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
