      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minOperations(s1: str, s2: str, x: int) -> int:\n    n = len(s1)\n    \n    # Find positions where s1 and s2 differ\n    diff = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if s1[i] != s2[i]:\n            diff.append(i)\n    \n    # If odd number of differences, it's impossible\n    if len(diff) % 2 == 1:\n        return -1\n    \n    # If no differences, already equal\n    if len(diff) == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Use dynamic programming to find minimum cost\n    # dp[i] represents minimum cost to fix first i differences\n    m = len(diff)\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (m + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        # Option 1: Use operation 1 (cost x) to fix current difference with any previous one\n        if i >= 2:\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i-2] + x)\n        \n        # Option 2: Use operation 2 to fix adjacent differences\n        # We can connect diff[i-1] with diff[i-2] if they're consecutive\n        if i >= 2:\n            gap = diff[i-1] - diff[i-2]\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i-2] + gap)\n    \n    return dp[m]\n```",
