      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    # Use a set to store unique substrings that are repetitions of one character\n    unique_substrings = set()\n    \n    # Iterate through the string to find consecutive character groups\n    i = 0\n    while i < N:\n        char = S[i]\n        count = 1\n        \n        # Count consecutive occurrences of the same character\n        while i + count < N and S[i + count] == char:\n            count += 1\n        \n        # For a group of 'count' consecutive characters, we can form\n        # substrings of length 1, 2, ..., count\n        # Each of these is a repetition of one character\n        for length in range(1, count + 1):\n            substring = char * length\n            unique_substrings.add(substring)\n        \n        i += count\n    \n    print(len(unique_substrings))\n\nsolve()\n```",
