    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a 0-indexed string num representing a non-negative integer.\nIn one operation, you can pick any digit of num and delete it. Note that if you delete all the digits of num, num becomes 0.\nReturn the minimum number of operations required to make num special.\nAn integer x is considered special if it is divisible by 25.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: num = \"2245047\"\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: Delete digits num[5] and num[6]. The resulting number is \"22450\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 2 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\nExample 2:\n\nInput: num = \"2908305\"\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: Delete digits num[3], num[4], and num[6]. The resulting number is \"2900\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 3 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\nExample 3:\n\nInput: num = \"10\"\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: Delete digit num[0]. The resulting number is \"0\" which is special since it is divisible by 25.\nIt can be shown that 1 is the minimum number of operations required to get a special number.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= num.length <= 100\nnum only consists of digits '0' through '9'.\nnum does not contain any leading zeros.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of operations to make a number divisible by 25 by deleting digits.\n\nA number is divisible by 25 if and only if its last two digits are 00, 25, 50, or 75. So I need to find the minimum deletions to make the number end with one of these valid suffixes.\n\nMy approach:\n1. For each valid suffix (00, 25, 50, 75), find if I can form that suffix from the given number\n2. For each valid suffix, find the rightmost occurrence of the second digit, then find the rightmost occurrence of the first digit that appears before the second digit\n3. Calculate the number of deletions needed (digits after the second digit + digits between first and second digit that need to be deleted)\n4. Return the minimum deletions across all valid suffixes\n5. Handle the special case where we can make the number 0 (by keeping just one '0')\n\n```python\ndef minimumOperations(num):\n    def find_min_deletions_for_suffix(target_suffix):\n        last_digit = target_suffix[1]\n        first_digit = target_suffix[0]\n        \n        # Find rightmost occurrence of last_digit\n        last_pos = -1\n        for i in range(len(num) - 1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == last_digit:\n                last_pos = i\n                break\n        \n        if last_pos == -1:\n            return float('inf')\n        \n        # Find rightmost occurrence of first_digit before last_pos\n        first_pos = -1\n        for i in range(last_pos - 1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == first_digit:\n                first_pos = i\n                break\n        \n        if first_pos == -1:\n            return float('inf')\n        \n        # Deletions needed = digits after last_pos + digits between first_pos and last_pos that we don't want\n        # Actually, we just need to delete everything after last_pos and everything between first_pos and last_pos except the first_digit\n        # But since we're keeping the two digits, we delete everything after last_pos and skip the first_digit before last_pos\n        deletions_after = len(num) - 1 - last_pos\n        deletions_between = last_pos - first_pos - 1\n        \n        return deletions_after + deletions_between\n    \n    min_ops = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try all valid suffixes for divisibility by 25\n    for suffix in [\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"]:\n        ops = find_min_deletions_for_suffix(suffix)\n        min_ops = min(min_ops, ops)\n    \n    # Special case: we can also make the number 0 by keeping just one '0'\n    # Find rightmost '0' and delete everything after it\n    for i in range(len(num) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if num[i] == '0':\n            # Keep this '0' and delete everything after it\n            ops_for_zero = len(num) - 1 - i\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, ops_for_zero)\n            break\n    \n    # If no valid configuration found, we might need to delete everything except make it 0\n    # But the problem states if we delete all digits, num becomes 0, which is divisible by 25\n    # So worst case is deleting all digits except we can always make 0\n    if min_ops == float('inf'):\n        # Check if there's at least one '0' to make the number 0\n        if '0' in num:\n            # Find rightmost '0'\n            rightmost_zero = len(num) - 1 - num[::-1].index('0')\n            min_ops = len(num) - 1 - rightmost_zero\n        else:\n            # No zeros, so we need to delete all digits to make it 0\n            min_ops = len(num)\n    \n    return min_ops\n```",
