      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    M = int(input())\n    S1 = input().strip()\n    S2 = input().strip()\n    S3 = input().strip()\n    \n    reels = [S1, S2, S3]\n    \n    min_time = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each digit from 0 to 9\n    for digit in '0123456789':\n        times = []\n        for reel in reels:\n            # Find all positions where this digit appears in the reel\n            positions = [i for i, c in enumerate(reel) if c == digit]\n            if not positions:\n                times = None\n                break\n            times.append(positions)\n        \n        if times is None:  # This digit doesn't appear in all reels\n            continue\n            \n        # Try all combinations of positions\n        for t1 in times[0]:\n            for t2 in times[1]:\n                for t3 in times[2]:\n                    # The actual time when each reel is stopped\n                    # t seconds gives us character at position (t mod M)\n                    # So to get character at position p, we need t such that t mod M = p\n                    # The earliest such t is p, then p+M, p+2M, etc.\n                    \n                    # We need to find the minimum total time where all reels are stopped\n                    # and the last reel is stopped at some time t\n                    possible_times = []\n                    \n                    # For each position p, the possible stopping times are p, p+M, p+2M, ...\n                    # We need to find a combination where all three times are achievable\n                    # and we minimize the maximum time (when the last reel is stopped)\n                    \n                    for offset1 in range(3):  # Check a few cycles\n                        time1 = t1 + offset1 * M\n                        for offset2 in range(3):\n                            time2 = t2 + offset2 * M\n                            for offset3 in range(3):\n                                time3 = t3 + offset3 * M\n                                \n                                # The total time is the maximum of the three\n                                total_time = max(time1, time2, time3)\n                                possible_times.append(total_time)\n                    \n                    if possible_times:\n                        min_possible = min(possible_times)\n                        min_time = min(min_time, min_possible)\n    \n    if min_time == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_time)\n\nsolve()\n```",
