      "generated_answer": "The zeros of \\(f(x)=\\sin(7\\pi\\sin(5x))\\) occur when \\(\\sin(5x)=k/7\\) for \\(k=-7,-6,\\dots,7\\). In \\((0,2\\pi)\\), each nonzero \\(k\\) with \\(|k|<7\\) gives 10 solutions, \\(k=0\\) gives 9 solutions, and \\(k=\\pm7\\) give 10 solutions, so \\(n=9+12\\cdot10+2\\cdot10=149\\). Tangency requires \\(f'(x)=0\\), which reduces to \\(\\cos(5x)=0\\) at a zero, so only the zeros with \\(\\sin(5x)=\\pm1\\) qualify; these are \\(x=\\pi/10+m\\pi/5\\) for \\(m=0,\\dots,9\\), giving \\(t=10\\). Thus \\(n+t=159\\).\n\n\\boxed{159}",
