      "generated_answer": "The limit can be evaluated using the Stolz–Cesàro theorem. Let \\(x_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n k a_k\\) and \\(y_n = n^2\\). Then \\(\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} x_n / y_n = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} (x_n - x_{n-1})/(y_n - y_{n-1}) = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} (n a_n)/(2n-1) = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} a_n/(2 - 1/n) = 1/2\\). Therefore, the correct answer is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
