      "generated_answer": "The flat-compound condition requires series field turns to provide additional magnetomotive force (MMF) of \\((7.0 - 4.5) \\times 750 = 1875\\) ampere-turns per pole. With a load current of 200 A in the short-shunt connection, the needed turns are \\(1875/200 = 9.375 \\approx 9.4\\). For part (b), with 12 turns per pole and total series field resistance \\(6 \\times 0.005 = 0.03\\,\\Omega\\), the required series current is \\(1875/12 = 156.25\\) A, leaving a diverter current of \\(200 - 156.25 = 43.75\\) A. The diverter resistance computes as \\((156.25 \\times 0.03)/43.75 = 0.107\\,\\Omega\\). Thus option H matches both values.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
